<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Container Orchestration with AWS EKS'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Container Orchestration with AWS EKS & Kubernetes</h1>
  <p>Deployed a six-microservice retail application on Amazon EKS using Terraform and Kustomize, exposed externally via AWS Network Load Balancer.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>EKS</span><span>Kubernetes</span><span>Terraform</span><span>Docker</span><span>kubectl</span><span>Kustomize</span><span>NLB</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/eks-kubernetes.png" alt="EKS Kubernetes Architecture Diagram" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates <strong>container orchestration</strong> using <strong>Amazon EKS</strong>, AWS's managed Kubernetes platform. A multi-microservice retail application was deployed and exposed to the internet.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Set up <strong>Cloud9 IDE</strong> environment using CloudFormation.</li>
      <li>Provisioned <strong>EKS cluster</strong> using Terraform (Infrastructure as Code).</li>
      <li>Deployed <strong>6 microservices</strong>: UI, Catalog, Carts, Checkout, Orders, Assets.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>Kubernetes deployments, services, and namespaces</strong>.</li>
      <li>Exposed the application using <strong>AWS Network Load Balancer</strong>.</li>
      <li>Scaled pods dynamically using <strong>kubectl scale</strong> commands.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>☸️ Kubernetes Layer</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Amazon EKS</strong> — Managed Kubernetes control plane</li>
          <li><strong>Worker Nodes (EC2)</strong> — Run containerized microservices</li>
          <li><strong>Namespaces</strong> — Isolation per microservice</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>📦 Microservices</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>UI, Catalog, Carts, Checkout, Orders, Assets</li>
          <li><strong>ClusterIP Services</strong> — Internal communication</li>
          <li><strong>StatefulSets</strong> — MySQL, RabbitMQ</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🌐 Networking</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Network Load Balancer</strong> — External traffic entry</li>
          <li><strong>AWS Load Balancer Controller</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Terraform</strong> — VPC, EKS, node groups</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Launched <strong>Cloud9 IDE</strong> using CloudFormation template.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Downloaded Terraform configs and ran <strong><code>terraform apply</code></strong> to create EKS cluster.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Configured <strong>kubectl</strong> using <code>aws eks update-kubeconfig</code>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Deployed Catalog microservice using <strong><code>kubectl apply -k</code></strong>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Scaled Catalog to <strong>3 replicas</strong> using <code>kubectl scale</code>.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">6</div><p>Deployed all remaining microservices and installed <strong>AWS Load Balancer Controller</strong>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Provisioned <strong>EKS cluster</strong> using Terraform for reproducible infrastructure.</li>
      <li>Understood Kubernetes concepts: <strong>Pods, Deployments, Services, Namespaces</strong>.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>Kustomize</strong> for managing Kubernetes manifests.</li>
      <li>Deployed <strong>StatefulSets</strong> for databases (MySQL, RabbitMQ).</li>
      <li>Exposed services using <strong>ClusterIP</strong> (internal) and <strong>LoadBalancer</strong> (external).</li>
      <li>Cleaned up resources using <strong>terraform destroy</strong> to avoid costs.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

